+# Technical Plan
+
+The implementation will extend the existing React screen and `subscriptionService` rather than introduce routing, global state, a component library, or a new test framework. The current repository is a client-side fixture application, so the service will model the billing boundary asynchronously and keep provider-shaped details out of the UI.
+
+## PLAN-001: Extend the domain model and fixtures
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-001, REQ-003, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007
+
+- In `src/types.ts`, add the minimal draft, preview, request-status, and safe-error types described by the specification state model. Replace the free-form `pendingChange?: string` with a structured optional change request.
+- In `src/data/subscriptions.ts`, migrate the existing pending fixture to the structured type and retain the three evidenced plans. Add only fixture values needed to exercise preview and final-result states.
+- Keep `renewalDate` as a date-only string and format it at display time without UTC conversion.
+
+## PLAN-002: Make the existing service the business-rule boundary
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007, REQ-008
+
+- Extend `src/services/subscriptionService.ts` with pure validation/classification helpers plus asynchronous `previewChange`, `submitChange`, and `reconcileChange` functions.
+- Enforce role permissions, the single-pending-request rule, preview validity, and effective timing in `submitChange`, even when the UI has already checked them.
+- Generate one idempotency key per confirmed submission with `crypto.randomUUID()` and retain it for unknown-outcome retries. Do not generate a replacement inside retry logic.
+- Return customer-safe error codes/messages from the service. Keep provider/internal error objects private to the service and map unknown failures to one generic recovery message.
+- Treat provider preview amounts and dates as authoritative. Do not implement local price or proration formulas.
+
+## PLAN-003: Add one inline management workflow
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007, REQ-008
+
+- Update `src/App.tsx` to own per-account draft, preview, submission, and feedback state with React state. Render the management form inline in the selected account card; only one card needs to be open at a time.
+- Use native `select`, `input type="number"`, and buttons. Derive allowed actions and disabled states from the account role and structured request status.
+- Use a two-step draft then confirmation flow. Changing any draft field clears the preview; confirmation displays provider amounts and effective date before calling submit.
+- On accepted submission, render pending state and poll the service's reconciliation function until a final fixture result is returned. On conflict, refresh the account request. On unknown outcome, expose a retry that reuses the retained key.
+- Update `src/styles.css` only for the form, status, error, disabled, and focus-visible states; retain the existing responsive card layout.
+
+## PLAN-004: Verify policy and observable flows
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007, REQ-008
+
+- Add a small Node built-in test script covering authorization, classification/timing, pending conflicts, safe error mapping, and idempotent retry. Wire it into the existing `npm test` command without adding a package.
+- Exercise each acceptance criterion against the three fixture roles and include final verification with `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`.
+- Verify keyboard focus, labels, live status/error announcements, and narrow-screen layout manually because the repository has no browser-test dependency.
+
+## Implementation sequence
+
+1. PLAN-001 establishes types and fixtures.
+2. PLAN-002 implements and tests the shared policy boundary.
+3. PLAN-003 connects the UI to that boundary.
+4. PLAN-004 runs traceable acceptance and repository checks.
+
+No route, backend server, approval engine, refund logic, cadence editor, or payment UI is added under this plan.
+
