+# Implementation Tasks
+
+Tasks are ordered so policy is testable before UI wiring. Each task includes its requirement and acceptance-criterion trace.
+
+## TASK-001: Define structured change state
+
+**Trace:** REQ-001, REQ-003, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007; AC-007, AC-008, AC-009, AC-012
+
+- Add draft, preview, change type/timing/status, and safe-error types in `src/types.ts`.
+- Migrate the pending account in `src/data/subscriptions.ts` from a string to a structured request and add the minimum fixture response data needed for final success and failure.
+- Confirm `npm run typecheck` passes before behavior changes begin.
+
+## TASK-002: Implement authorization and draft validation
+
+**Trace:** REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-008; AC-001, AC-002, AC-003, AC-013
+
+- Add pure permission, validation, and increase/decrease classification helpers to `src/services/subscriptionService.ts`.
+- Enforce owner, billing-admin, viewer, cancellation, positive-integer seat, unchanged-draft, mixed-direction, and Enterprise-without-approval rules at the service boundary.
+- Add Node built-in checks for every role and invalid draft class.
+
+## TASK-003: Implement authoritative preview behavior
+
+**Trace:** REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-007; AC-003, AC-004, AC-005, AC-006, AC-010
+
+- Add asynchronous preview behavior to `src/services/subscriptionService.ts` using fixture provider results.
+- Return immediate timing and provider-supplied proration for increases; return renewal-date timing and zero due now for decreases and cancellation.
+- Map preview failures to safe codes/messages and prove raw provider details cannot reach the returned preview error.
+
+## TASK-004: Implement submission, pending, and reconciliation
+
+**Trace:** REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007; AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-011, AC-012
+
+- Add submit and reconciliation behavior to `src/services/subscriptionService.ts`, including preview-token validation, service-side permissions, one-pending-request enforcement, accepted-versus-final status, and structured success/failure updates.
+- Create the idempotency key once with `crypto.randomUUID()` and preserve the body and key for an unknown-outcome retry; start a new key only after a reconciled terminal failure and a fresh preview.
+- Add built-in checks proving one accepted request, conflict refresh, same-key retry, final success, terminal failure recovery, and safe error mapping.
+
+## TASK-005: Build the accessible management form and preview
+
+**Trace:** REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-007, REQ-008; AC-001, AC-002, AC-003, AC-004, AC-005, AC-006, AC-013
+
+- In `src/App.tsx`, add one inline form using native controls for allowed plan, seat, and cancellation actions.
+- Hide disallowed actions, disable mutation for blocking states, show inline validation, invalidate stale previews, and format preview currency/date with `Intl`.
+- Add labels, focus movement, live regions, and visible focus/error styles in `src/styles.css`; retain the existing responsive layout.
+
+## TASK-006: Connect request lifecycle and recovery UI
+
+**Trace:** REQ-001, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007; AC-007, AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-011, AC-012
+
+- Connect confirmation to submit, prevent repeat clicks, show accepted work as pending, and reconcile to applied or failed.
+- Refresh the existing pending request on conflict. Expose same-key retry only for an unknown outcome and fresh-preview retry only after reconciled terminal failure.
+- Ensure every rendered failure is the service's safe message and current subscription data remains unchanged on rejection or failure.
+
+## TASK-007: Run acceptance and repository verification
+
+**Trace:** REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006, REQ-007, REQ-008; AC-001, AC-002, AC-003, AC-004, AC-005, AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-011, AC-012, AC-013
+
+- Run the built-in policy checks, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`.
+- Walk through AC-001 through AC-013 using the owner, billing-admin, viewer, and pending fixtures, recording pass/fail results.
+- Check keyboard-only operation, focus placement, announced status/error content, narrow viewport behavior, absence of raw provider details, and absence of out-of-scope controls.
+

